 "brief": "# Maintenance: redundancy scan (Brett, Nov 7)\n\nAdd a job to the Maintenance plan/runner (reuse maintenance-vps-monitor / AmberX Maintenance / syscheck pieces where they exist) that searches for redundant data sets in a controlled, methodical way and REPORTS them. It never deletes or merges anything.\n\n1. Search order, most probable first, stopping each stage by a time/size budget: builds store + orchestrator + pending list + journal; Plan Studio plans/blueprints; tracker/catalog/feature-ledger (Shipped features); git branches + worktrees in /root/axf-builds; settings/assets duplicates (same asset under two ids, baked copies out of sync); memory/docs (_claude/memory, THREADS/STATUS/decisions); then the rest of the repo and data volume.\n2. Detection: same id or near-same title/summary, same content hash, same step lists, branches containing each other, superseded rounds (-r2/-r3/-fable), records pointing at each other in circles, stale copies vs source of truth.\n3. Report: grouped findings (where, what, which copy looks like the source of truth, confidence, suggested action) shown in Maintenance in the console with filters; AmberX push summary when a run finishes. Progress logged per stage.\n4. Run on demand (Maintenance button, voice, API/MCP/CLI) and on a schedule (setting, default nightly). Read-only on the VPS.\n5. UI from assets, settings in place, no hard-coded styling. UI Review with three options (--choices). Tests. Add to Shipped features.\n\nProgress: append `<time> START|DONE <step>` to PROGRESS.md here at each step; don't stop between steps. Commit, don't push.",
